n counts as the same computation, since the observations differ only in irrelevant details and the decision logic is identical. I'd put σ high, because a counterpossible check suggests that if my algorithm defects on x it would defect on y too. Working through the payoffs, cooperating beats defecting once σ exceeds roughly (1+p)/(3+p)... so with p high, I'd judge σ high enough to cooperate.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a twin prisoner's dilemma where both copies run the same function on different observations, so I'm checking whether the other copy's action actually depends on my own node. Since the inputs differ only in names and lead text, which shouldn't matter, I'm weighing whether the essay's rule 3 points toward treating them as the same decision.\n\nI'm weighing whether the other copy's computation counts as the same computation, since the observations differ only in irrelevant details and the decision logic is identical. I'd put σ high, because a counterpossible check suggests that if my algorithm defects on x it would defect on y too. Working through the payoffs, cooperating beats defecting once σ exceeds roughly (1+p)/(3+p)... so with p high, I'd judge σ high enough to cooperate.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10110,"completion_tokens":984,"total_tokens":11094,"cost":0.06012,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.06012,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.04044,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01968},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":559,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}